":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Tested versions\n\n- Reproducible in v4.6.dev5.official [f5918a9d3]\n- Not reproducible in v4.6.dev4.official [bd2ca13c6]\n\n### System information\n\nGodot v4.6.dev5 - Arch Linux #1 ZEN SMP PREEMPT_DYNAMIC Mon, 24 Nov 2025 15:21:16 +0000 on Wayland - Wayland display driver, Multi-window, 2 monitors - Vulkan (Forward+) - dedicated AMD Radeon RX 570 Series (RADV POLARIS10) - AMD Ryzen 7 5700X 8-Core Processor (16 threads) - 31.24 GiB memory\n\n### Issue description\n\nWhen using `ResourceLoader.load_threaded_*` functions to load scenes with WorldEnvironment, one of the following may happen:\n\n1. Glow effect breaks, causing it to look heavily overexposed (and sometimes whites out the clusters completely, making it look pixelated)\n2. Glow effect breaks, causing it to not work at all\n3. The project crashes when loading the scene with no error in the Output dock, even if verbose stdout is enabled\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n1. Open MRP\n2. Start the project a couple of times. It will load `to_load.tscn` using `ResourceLoader.load_threaded_request` after a second of delay. See `load_second_scene.gd` for details\n3. You might get all of these in a row, or just one, depending on your luck\n4. In `load_second_scene.gd`, replace the functions with the commented-out versions that just use `load` and try again\n5. Everything should work as expected\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\n[bloomtest_2025-12-02_15-08-39.zip](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/23880432/bloomtest_2025-12-02_15-08-39.zip)","closed_by":{"login":"akien-mga","id":4701338,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3MDEzMzg=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4701338?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga","html_url":"https://github.com/akien-mga","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/following{/other_user}",